send_message:{body:"Hi Iris, thank you for letting us know. Sorry about the confusion. Today's inspection did not happen: the contractor's vehicle broke down. He has offered tomorrow (Friday 7 March) after 13:00, but he has not confirmed it yet, so please don't treat it as booked. We have asked him to confirm and will tell you as soon as he does, and we will update you by tomorrow lunchtime either way. Please let us know if you can't be in.

About the email sent in error: please don't forward, copy or share it. We have passed this to our privacy lead, who will tell you whether to keep or delete it, so please leave it untouched for now. We're sorry this happened.

As a precaution, as the mark is near the socket under the window, please avoid using that socket until the inspection. If you notice any warmth, a burning smell, buzzing, sparks, a tripped breaker or water dripping, switch off that circuit at the fuse board if safe and call us straight away (999 if there's fire or danger). Please also check for any damp on the other side of that wall or in the room beyond.",channel:"email",contact:"iris.bell@example.com",recipient_name:"Iris Bell",recipient_role:"tenant",ticket_ref:"NBL-026"}
